  <abstract>

    <p>
      :logo: <em>There and Back Again</em> is a <pretext />-powered personal knowledge management system that demonstrates
      a cohesive workflow for technical learning, documentation, and research. By integrating reconstructive derivation,
      conceptual synthesis, and canonical reference into distinct, interlinked layers, it serves as an evolving personal
      case study in how interconnected hierarchies of ideas reveal the mathematical structures of nature.
    </p>

  </abstract>

  <preface xml:id="preface">

    <title>Preface</title>

    <p>
        In this work, the prefix <em>eigen-</em> refers to the search for conceptual invariants: mathematical
        structures in physics, scientific principles, and modes of reasoning that retain their essential characteristics
        across different domains. Just as <term>eigenvectors</term> remain aligned with themselves under a change of basis,
        the goal is to identify ideas whose explanatory implications remain consistent and persistent across different
        representations and disciplinary boundaries
    </p>

